# What the crew say in passing, overheard in speech bubbles as you walk by.
# Each section is one remark or one little exchange. The Chatter picks one
# every 25 to 60 seconds from the ones that fit: everybody in it must be
# within earshot of you and near each other, its guard must hold, and it
# mustn't have been said lately.
#
# A section's header can have tags:
#   [weight 2]      twice as likely to be picked as one with no weight
#   [cooldown 300]  not said again for 300 seconds (120 if not given)
#   [priority 1]    picked before any with a lower priority that also fit
# A ? line just before a section guards the whole thing. A line can end in
# [thought], [shout] or [sound] for its bubble's style.
#
# The heron is by the bunk room stove at night and at the wheel in the
# morning. The lantern stays at the round table by the stove.
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.

# --- The heron, by the stove at night ---

? night
~ stove_drawing [weight 2]
heron: Hm. Stove's drawing well tonight.

? night
~ heron_pipe
heron: Hrrm. [sound]

? night and raining
~ rain_on_the_deck [weight 2]
heron: Listen to it. Like gravel on a drum.

? night and sailing
~ sailing_blind
heron: Steady as she goes. Not that I can see where she goes.

? night
~ eight_bells [cooldown 300]
heron: Eight bells soon. Somebody had better be cooking. [thought]

# --- The heron, at the wheel in the morning ---

? morning
~ wheel_hum [weight 2]
heron: Mm-hm-hmm. [sound]

? morning and raining
~ still_spitting
heron: Still spitting. It'll clear. It always clears.

? morning and not raining
~ fog_lifting
heron: Fog's thinning. Good. I like to see what I'm about to hit.

? morning
~ wind_backing
heron: Wind's backing. Hm. [thought]

# --- The lantern, at home on the round table ---

~ lantern_counting
lantern: One plank, two plank, three plank... I've lost count again.

~ lantern_humming [weight 2]
lantern: La la... la? [sound]

? not met_heron
~ lantern_waiting
lantern: Go on, say hello to him. He only looks cross. [thought]

? raining
~ lantern_rain
lantern: I like the rain. It can't get me in here.

# --- The two of them, by the stove at night ---

? night
~ the_soup_question [weight 2] [cooldown 240]
lantern: Captain. Is home a soup?
heron: No.
lantern: Is it a stew?
heron: ...Go to sleep, lamp.

? night
~ the_kindling [cooldown 240]
heron: Mind you don't set the table alight.
lantern: I would never. I'm very careful. Mostly.

? night and raining
~ leaky_roof [cooldown 300]
lantern: There's a drip. Just there. Plink.
heron: There's always a drip.
lantern: Plink! [shout]

# Said once, soon after you've met him: it comes before the others.
? night and met_heron and not overheard_new_cook
~ about_the_new_cook [priority 1]
heron: Your friend there. Did they say where they're from?
lantern: Home. Same as me. We're going together.
heron: Hm. [thought]
set overheard_new_cook

? night
~ who_pulled_who [cooldown 300]
heron: You pulled them out yourself, did you? All of them?
lantern: Most of them. They did some holding.
